{"name":"Home Song","hex":"#f2eec7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"home","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dwelling.\nOne’s own dwelling place; the house or structure in which one lives; especially the house in which one lives with one's family; the habitual abode of one’s family.\n\nThe place (residence, settlement, country, etc.), where a person was born or raised; a childhood or parental home; the home of one’s parents or guardian.","One’s own dwelling place; the house or structure in which one lives; especially the house in which one lives with one's family; the habitual abode of one’s family."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To return to its owner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/home"},{"term":"song","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical composition with lyrics for voice or voices, performed by singing.","Any musical composition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/song"}],"entries":[{"title":"Home","blocks":[{"text":"A home, or domicile, is a space used as a permanent or semi-permanent residence for one or more human occupants, and sometimes various companion animals. Homes provide sheltered spaces, for instance rooms, where domestic activity can be performed such as sleeping, preparing food, eating, and hygiene as well as providing spaces for work and leisure such as remote working, studying, and playing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/SearsHouse115.jpg/330px-SearsHouse115.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home","wikidata":"Q7743"},{"title":"Song","blocks":[{"text":"A song is a musical composition performed by the human voice. The voice often carries the melody using patterns of sound and silence. Songs have a structure, such as the common ABA form, and are usually made of sections that are repeated or performed with variation later. A song without instruments is said to be a cappella."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Billie_Holiday%2C_Downbeat%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Feb._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_04251%29.jpg/330px-Billie_Holiday%2C_Downbeat%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Feb._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_04251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song","wikidata":"Q7366"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Taino_petroglyph_in_cave.jpg/500px-Taino_petroglyph_in_cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Taino_petroglyph_in_cave.jpg/500px-Taino_petroglyph_in_cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Taíno petroglyphs in a cave in Puerto Rico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaino_petroglyph_in_cave.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Worker_home_from_1911_in_Helsinki.jpg/500px-Worker_home_from_1911_in_Helsinki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Worker_home_from_1911_in_Helsinki.jpg/1280px-Worker_home_from_1911_in_Helsinki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Worker_home_from_1911_in_Helsinki.jpg/500px-Worker_home_from_1911_in_Helsinki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Industrialization brought mass migration to cities. This one-room worker home from Helsinki is typical to late 19th century and early 20th century, often housing large families.[18]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorker_home_from_1911_in_Helsinki.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/8A%2C_Bulevardul_Avi